.Dd November 13, 2026
.Dt EIGRP 8
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm eigrp
.Nd inspect and administer the native OpenEIGRP daemon
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Ar options
.Cm show
.Op Cm address-family Ar ipv4|ipv6 Op Cm vrf Ar name
.Op Ar asn
.Ar view
.Op Ar arguments
.Nm
.Op Ar options
.Cm clear
.Op Cm address-family Ar ipv4|ipv6 Op Cm vrf Ar name
.Op Ar asn
.Ar target
.Op Ar arguments
.Nm
.Op Ar options
.Cm version
.Nm
.Cm help
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
is a noninteractive client for
.Xr openeigrpd 8 .
It sends bounded, versioned requests to the local Unix management socket.
The text renderer uses Cisco IOS/IOS XE style headings and column layouts
where portable management snapshots contain the required data.
Missing host/Cisco-specific fields are identified rather than fabricated.
The machine-readable JSON records are unchanged.
.Sh COMMANDS
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Cm show version
Show the client, host, and portable-component version inventory.
.It Cm show capabilities
Report protocol release and supported capabilities.
.It Cm show protocols
List configured EIGRP instances and runtime status.
.It Cm show neighbors Op Cm detail Op Ar interface
Show neighbors and their hold time, uptime, queues, SRTT, RTO and sequence numbers.
.It Cm show interfaces Op Cm detail Op Ar interface
Show EIGRP interface settings, peer counts, and operational counters.
.It Cm show topology Op Cm all-links | Ar prefix
Show DUAL prefixes and paths. The default human-readable view selects
successor and feasible-successor paths; all-links includes the other paths.
.It Cm show statistics
Show portable traffic counters.
.Cm traffic
is an alias.
.It Cm show events
Show event-log summary and entries.
.It Cm show diagnostics
Show feature capability, debug and timer records.
.It Cm show tech-support
Collect version, protocol inventory and available scoped read-only views.
.Cm tech-support
is an alias.
.It Cm clear events
Reset the event history of matching instances.
.It Cm clear neighbors Op Ar interface|address Op Cm soft
Reset EIGRP neighbor adjacencies using the portable administrative API.
A soft clear may preserve an adjacency, as determined by the portable core.
.It Cm clear topology Op Ar prefix
Clear all topology entries or one selected prefix through the portable core.
.It Cm version
Show local integration release, OS, kernel and IPC version without a daemon.
.It Cm help
Print usage.
.El
.Sh INSTANCE SELECTION
An omitted autonomous-system number selects every matching AS.
An omitted address-family selects both IPv4 and IPv6.
When neither is given, all running default-VRF address families are selected.
Command keywords allow unambiguous leading abbreviations such as
.Cm show addr ipv4 topo .
Ambiguous abbreviations return an error; names and addresses are not
abbreviated.
The
.Cm vrf default
selector is supported.
Other named Linux VRFs cannot currently be resolved through the native
control interface and are rejected; an explicit numeric nondefault
.Fl -vrf-id
requires both ASN and AFI.
.Sh OPTIONS
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl s Ar path , Fl -socket Ar path
Unix management socket; default
.Pa /run/openeigrpd/control.sock .
.It Fl a Ar asn , Fl -asn Ar asn
Filter to autonomous system 1 through 65535.
.It Fl 4 , Fl 6
Select IPv4 or IPv6.
.It Fl -afi Ar 4|6
Select an address family numerically.
.It Fl -vrf-id Ar number
Explicit numeric runtime VRF ID; default 0.
.It Fl -json
Emit unmodified newline-delimited JSON records, rather than text output.
The detail and positional interface/prefix display filters are not available
in JSON mode.
.It Fl h , Fl -help
Print usage.
.It Fl -version
Print local version and exit.
.El
.Sh EXAMPLES
.Bd -literal -offset indent
eigrp show nei
eigrp show address-family ipv4 4453 topology
eigrp show addr ipv6 topo
eigrp show address-family ipv4 4453 interfaces detail eth0
eigrp show 4453 traffic --json
sudo eigrp clear address-family ipv4 4453 neighbors 192.0.2.2
sudo eigrp clear topology 192.0.2.0/24
sudo eigrp clear events
.Ed
.Sh OUTPUT
Human-readable output is organized per matching EIGRP AF and AS.
The command is not a Linux kernel RIB viewer; use
.Xr ip 8
for host routes.
A request for
.Cm show routes
is rejected explicitly.
The original machine-readable record format and fields are preserved for
normal scoped views and technical-support JSON.
The daemon has no stable cross-page snapshot guarantee; topology changes
can affect subsequent pages.
.Sh SECURITY
The control socket is normally mode 0660 and belongs to the
.Sy openeigrpctl
access group. Read-only clients require socket access but not root.
Every
.Cm clear
request is authorized separately using peer credentials; only root or
the daemon startup UID may invoke a modifying operation.
No interactive configuration or live configuration reload is exposed.
.Sh LIMITATIONS
Management IPC version 2 pages contain at most 32 records and 16 KiB.
Page offsets are bounded at 8192; large topology dumps may therefore
return a pagination error.
Named nondefault Linux VRFs and byte-identical Cisco output across other
host integrations are not supported by this client alone.
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It 0
Success.
.It 1
Daemon, socket, authorization, instance selection or protocol failure.
.It 2
Invalid command line or unsupported command.
.El
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr openeigrpd 8 ,
.Xr openeigrpd.conf 5
